# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Synthetic example graphs authored within the GraphInOut project (Calpano)
# These exercise specific Graphviz DOT features; several mirror constructs
# from the Graphviz documentation/gallery.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

example.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example.dot ..format.. format:dot
example.dot ..content.. Tiny commutative-diagram-style digraph (A1..A3 / B1..B3) with two rank=same rows.
example.dot ..tests.. rank=same subgraph blocks, edge labels, tailport/headport on an edge, plaintext node shape
example.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example.dot ..license.. not stated

example2.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example2.dot ..format.. format:dot
example2.dot ..content.. Three shaped nodes (diamond/box/circle) plus an implicitly declared node D.
example2.dot ..tests.. node shape attributes, edge styling (dashed/penwidth/arrowhead=none), multi-color edge color "black:invis:black"
example2.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example2.dot ..license.. not stated

example3.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example3.dot ..format.. format:dot
example3.dot ..content.. Two nodes demonstrating record vs plaintext shape label semantics.
example3.dot ..tests.. shape=record label syntax with {|} fields, shape=plaintext where braces/bars are literal text
example3.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example3.dot ..license.. not stated

example4--INVALIDdot.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example4--INVALIDdot.dot ..format.. format:dot
example4--INVALIDdot.dot ..content.. Three record nodes a->b->c whose labels use \l (left), \n (newline) and \r (right) justification escapes.
example4--INVALIDdot.dot ..tests.. negative test: the DOT syntax is itself valid (and renders in some online tools), but it triggers a known parsing issue in JGraphT (see https://github.com/jgrapht/jgrapht/issues/1131); the "--INVALIDdot" marker flags it as a deliberate negative/regression case for the reader.
example4--INVALIDdot.dot ..depicts.. \l / \n / \r line-justification escapes inside record labels
example4--INVALIDdot.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example4--INVALIDdot.dot ..license.. not stated

example5.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example5.dot ..format.. format:dot
example5.dot ..content.. A parent node with an HTML-like table label exposing three ports, each linking to a child node.
example5.dot ..tests.. HTML-like (<...>) label tables, table cell ports, edges to ports via parent:port_one syntax
example5.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example5.dot ..license.. not stated

example6.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example6.dot ..format.. format:dot
example6.dot ..content.. A task/kanban-style graph where each node is an HTML table card (task title, description, colored done/todo status).
example6.dot ..tests.. HTML-like label tables with <b>/<font color=...> markup, cellborder/cellspacing/align attributes
example6.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example6.dot ..license.. not stated

example7.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example7.dot ..format.. format:dot
example7.dot ..content.. Small two-row layout (rA/sA/tA and uB/vB/wB) with implicitly declared nodes t and u.
example7.dot ..tests.. rank=same blocks, record-shaped node default, implicit node declaration via edges
example7.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example7.dot ..license.. not stated

example8.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example8.dot ..format.. format:dot
example8.dot ..content.. A node chain nd_1..nd_4 with extra nodes positioned around nd_3 inside a cluster.
example8.dot ..tests.. chained edges (a -> b -> c -> d), rank=same inside a named cluster subgraph, edge styling on grouped edges
example8.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example8.dot ..license.. not stated

example9.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example9.dot ..format.. format:dot
example9.dot ..content.. Nested cluster hierarchy: Parent > Child one (> Grand-Child one/two) and Child two, each holding plain nodes.
example9.dot ..tests.. deeply nested subgraph clusters with labels, bare node declarations
example9.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example9.dot ..license.. not stated

example9--SMALL.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example9--SMALL.dot ..format.. format:dot
example9--SMALL.dot ..content.. Trimmed minimal variant of example9.dot: bare nested clusters (cluster_BBB > cluster_CCC > cluster_DDD) with no labels.
example9--SMALL.dot ..tests.. minimal nested-cluster parsing (label-less subgraphs); the "--SMALL" marker flags it as a reduced/minimal variant of example9.dot
example9--SMALL.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example9--SMALL.dot ..license.. not stated

example10.dot ..kind.. synthetic
example10.dot ..format.. format:dot
example10.dot ..content.. Single node with a complex nested HTML-like table label (tables within table cells, colspan/rowspan, colors, <br/>).
example10.dot ..tests.. nested HTML-like label tables, colspan/rowspan, cellpadding/cellspacing/color attributes, <br/> and UTF-8 content (fünf)
example10.dot ..authored by.. Calpano (graphinout)
example10.dot ..license.. not stated
